WEBVTT

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:09.777
An agent is more than its model. Its harness supplies
prompts, tools, memory and workflow.

00:00:09.997 --> 00:00:15.649
Google Research's Harness² changes this surrounding
system while keeping model weights fixed.

00:00:15.869 --> 00:00:23.014
For the current task, propose harness edits, probe them
through execution, then compose a refinement from the
differences.

00:00:23.234 --> 00:00:29.995
Parallel recursion explores alternatives. Sequential
recursion carries a refinement into the next step.

00:00:30.215 --> 00:00:35.887
A second loop retains adopted harnesses and
evidence-supported lessons for future tasks.

00:00:36.107 --> 00:00:44.683
The official local demo fixes a ledger script that
ignores negative amounts. Scripted editors make this
example deterministic.

00:00:44.903 --> 00:00:49.029
It demonstrates the workflow, not a model learning to
solve new tasks.

00:00:49.249 --> 00:00:57.313
Start with the local demo. Model-backed experiments
need a cost budget, isolated execution and controlled
network access.
